## Project Motivation

My professional background is primarily in Identity and Access Management. I created this project to explore how my understanding of underlying IAM processes and technical controls could be translated into evidence that is meaningful from an investigation, audit, and compliance perspective.

The project focuses on a practical question:

> If an IAM workflow indicates that access was removed, how can we verify that the intended security state actually exists across downstream systems?

Using a synthetic IAM offboarding scenario, the project explores how evidence can be collected, reconciled, organized chronologically, documented into findings, connected to potentially relevant compliance controls, and tracked through remediation.
